  'tour.step.account.blurb': 'Your photo, name and password, switching accounts, and — for admins — managing users. Each user has their own library',
  'tour.step.account.em1.label': 'Profile',
  'tour.step.account.more': 'Admins add and remove users and grant admin here. The last admin cannot step down; to hand over, make someone else admin first. Switching accounts always asks for that account\'s password.',
  'tour.step.account.name': 'Profile & users',
  'tour.step.account.prose': 'The avatar opens your {em1} — photo, name, password, switching accounts and logging out. Every user has a separate library.',
  'tour.step.account.title': 'Yours, and everyone else’s',
  'tour.step.add.blurb': 'The ＋ button adds books, films and shows, captures quotes, and imports highlights in bulk',
  'tour.step.add.em1.label': 'book',
  'tour.step.add.em2.label': 'film or show',
  'tour.step.add.em3.label': 'quote',
  'tour.step.add.em4.label': 'import',
  'tour.step.add.more': 'Books are looked up by title, author or ISBN, films on TMDB and TheTVDB, with covers and details filled in. Imports read Markdown, Readest, Kindle, Goodreads, Hardcover and IMDb quote pages, and land in Pending import until you approve them there. Importing the same file twice never duplicates anything.',
  'tour.step.add.name': 'Add & import',
  'tour.step.add.prose': 'The ＋ button adds everything, and adapts to where you are: a {em1} on Library, a {em2} on the Catalogue, a {em3} on an open work. Bulk {em4} is a tab of the same panel.',
  'tour.step.add.title': 'One ＋ Add for everything',
  'tour.step.anthologies.blurb': 'quotes gathered into a reading order, with your own words between them',
  'tour.step.anthologies.em1.label': 'writing',
  'tour.step.anthologies.more': 'A quote can be in any number of anthologies and stays where it lives. Choose what each passage shows; let it keep filling and new matches are waiting when you open it. Export as Markdown or EPUB.',
  'tour.step.anthologies.name': 'Anthologies',
  'tour.step.anthologies.prose': 'An anthology is {em1}, not a shelf: quotes in your chosen order, with your own words between them. Point one at a book, tag, author or colour and it fills itself.',
  'tour.step.anthologies.title': 'Make something out of them',
  'tour.step.appearance.blurb': 'paper or film, light/dark/system, four accents — per user',
  'tour.step.appearance.name': 'Appearance',
  'tour.step.appearance.prose': 'Light, dark or match your system, your colours, a material set and cover sizes — each user keeps their own.',
  'tour.step.appearance.title': 'Make it yours',
  'tour.step.backup.blurb': 'one dated, encrypted archive, restored here or on another server; updates on demand (admin)',
  'tour.step.backup.em1.label': 'encrypted',
  'tour.step.backup.more': 'The archive includes password hashes and API keys, so it is encrypted. Your password opens it on any Tippani, or set a separate passphrase. The key is never stored, so keep it safe. Updates are checked only when you ask.',
  'tour.step.backup.name': 'Backup, restore & updates',
  'tour.step.backup.prose': 'One click makes a dated archive of everything, {em1} with your password. Restore it here, or on another Tippani to move.',
  'tour.step.backup.title': 'Sleep well',
  'tour.step.bin.blurb': 'what you deleted, restorable, until it ages out',
  'tour.step.bin.em1.label': 'restoring',
  'tour.step.bin.more': 'Each row shows what it was and when it was deleted. Remove one now, or empty the bin; otherwise items expire after the number of days set here.',
  'tour.step.bin.name': 'Bin',
  'tour.step.bin.prose': 'Deleted things wait here first — a book with its quotes, a film with its lines, or a single highlight — and {em1} puts it back.',
  'tour.step.bin.title': 'Nothing goes straight out',
  'tour.step.boards.blurb': 'lines that belong to no book and no film, filed on boards',
  'tour.step.boards.em1.label': 'boards',
  'tour.step.boards.more': 'A plain board holds anything; a proverb board pairs the original with a transliteration and a translation. Filter, group and export one board at a time. Deleting a board asks what to do with its quotes.',
  'tour.step.boards.name': 'Boards',
  'tour.step.boards.prose': 'A speech, a letter, a song, a proverb, something a friend said. They go on {em1} here — you choose the board as you save the line.',
  'tour.step.boards.title': 'Lines from everywhere else',
  'tour.step.book.blurb': 'its details, its highlights, and what you can do to both',
  'tour.step.book.em1.label': 'a quote against this book',
  'tour.step.book.more': 'The counts are filters, the ♥ marks the book or a single quote, and the shelf chip shows whether you\'re reading it. Copy, share and export work on one highlight or a selection.',
  'tour.step.book.name': 'A book\'s own page',
  'tour.step.book.prose': 'The book\'s details at the top and every highlight below. ＋ here adds {em1}, not another book.',
  'tour.step.book.title': 'Everything about one book',
  'tour.step.catalogue.blurb': 'memorable lines with timestamp, character and auto-filled actor',
  'tour.step.catalogue.more': 'The actor is filled in from the cast, so you only type the character. Shows add a season and episode. Tags, favourites, views and grouping work as in the Library.',
  'tour.step.catalogue.name': 'Catalogue — films & dialogues',
  'tour.step.catalogue.prose': 'Films and shows keep their dialogue the same way, each line with its timestamp and character. A line looks like this:',
  'tour.step.catalogue.title': 'The Catalogue',
  'tour.step.checks.blurb': 'the two lists waiting on you — imports, and quotes that look odd',
  'tour.step.checks.em1.label': 'odd',
  'tour.step.checks.more': 'Each list also has its own screen and link. This is about whether the text is right, not about remembering it.',
  'tour.step.checks.name': 'Checks',
  'tour.step.checks.prose': 'Two lists on one screen: imported quotes waiting for approval, and quotes where something looks {em1}.',
  'tour.step.checks.title': 'What is waiting on you',
  'tour.step.cleanup.blurb': 'what the page left on your quotes — page numbers, broken hyphens, footnote marks',
  'tour.step.cleanup.em1.label': 'page',
  'tour.step.cleanup.more': 'It only lists what it finds; nothing changes by itself. Filter by rule, open a row to fix it, and run again for the rest of a very large library.',
  'tour.step.cleanup.name': 'Cleanup',
  'tour.step.cleanup.prose': 'Reads every quote for things that came from the {em1}, not the writer: a stray page number, a hyphen from a line break, a footnote mark.',
  'tour.step.cleanup.title': 'What the page left behind',
  'tour.step.done.em1.label': 'one screen at a time',
  'tour.step.done.em2.label': '?',
  'tour.step.done.prose': 'That\'s everything. The {em2} on any screen explains its controls, and replays the tour there — it now runs {em1}. Enjoy.',
  'tour.step.done.title': 'That’s the tour',
  'tour.step.film.blurb': 'cast, credits and every line you kept',
  'tour.step.film.em1.label': 'the speakers',
  'tour.step.film.more': 'A speaker typed as a name can be mapped onto the cast, so their chip opens a person. Voice cast is kept separate. ＋ here adds a line to this film.',
  'tour.step.film.name': 'A film\'s own page',
  'tour.step.film.prose': 'Studio, publisher and the cast that {em1} match against, with every line you\'ve kept below.',
  'tour.step.film.title': 'Everything about one film',
  'tour.step.filters.blurb': 'field chips, scopes and dates over the results',
  'tour.step.filters.em1.label': 'two chips',
  'tour.step.filters.more': 'Type a backslash before a colon you mean literally. Colour names, a date and a decade all work, and coming from a filtered shelf brings its filters along. Select results to tag, recolour or add to an anthology.',
  'tour.step.filters.name': 'Search filters',
  'tour.step.filters.prose': 'Type a field and a colon — tag, author, colour — and the box suggests what you have. Chips stack, so {em1} narrow the results; the row above shows which part of the library you\'re searching.',
  'tour.step.filters.title': 'Narrow it down',
  'tour.step.keys.blurb': 'TMDB/TheTVDB/Google Books keys and the optional Amazon cookie (admin)',
  'tour.step.keys.more': 'TMDB (films and shows) usually works out of the box on a shared key. TheTVDB is optional and often better for long-running shows. Google Books only needs a key past about 1,000 lookups a day. The Amazon cookie is optional. Books need no key at all.',
  'tour.step.keys.name': 'Metadata keys & Amazon cookie',
  'tour.step.keys.prose': 'Lookups use the keys in the highlighted card. Each field saves on its own, and its info dot says where to get that key. Paste them now or press Next and add them later.',
  'tour.step.keys.title': 'Metadata keys & the Amazon cookie',
  'tour.step.library.blurb': 'Covers, series, colours, tags and favourites, shown as tiles, a list or a table, and grouped as you like',
  'tour.step.library.more': 'Each highlight has a colour, tags, a chapter and location, and a ♥. View as masonry, list or table; filter by genre, shelf, favourites, tags or notes; group by series, author, decade or genre.',
  'tour.step.library.name': 'Library — books & annotations',
  'tour.step.library.prose': 'Your books, with their covers and every highlight you\'ve kept. A highlight looks like this:',
  'tour.step.library.title': 'The Library',
  'tour.step.metadata.blurb': 'coverage per field, bulk fixes, duplicate merges; people with portraits & links',
  'tour.step.metadata.em1.label': 'People',
  'tour.step.metadata.more': 'Each coverage count is a filter: tap “no cover” to list just those books. Then correct a selection at once, merge duplicates, map speaker labels onto a cast, or re-check works against their sources before anything changes.',
  'tour.step.metadata.name': 'Metadata console & People',
  'tour.step.metadata.prose': 'Shows what the library is missing and fixes it in bulk. {em1} get photos and reference links — tap any author or actor name.',
  'tour.step.metadata.title': 'Keep the shelves tidy',
  'tour.step.quiz.blurb': 'spaced repetition over your quotes — cards resurface as you start to forget',
  'tour.step.quiz.more': 'Each quote has a status dot — remembered, forgetting or probably forgotten — and your answers move it. Practice is unlimited and skippable, with its own score, and leaves the schedule alone by default. Card count and the rest are in Settings.',
  'tour.step.quiz.name': 'Daily Quiz & Practice',
  'tour.step.quiz.prose': 'Home gives you a short daily quiz on your own quotes, each coming back just as you\'d start to forget it. Two or three minutes a day.',
  'tour.step.quiz.title': 'The daily ritual',
  'tour.step.search.blurb': 'typo-tolerant full-text search across quotes, works, people and notes',
  'tour.step.search.em1.label': 'typo-tolerant',
  'tour.step.search.more': 'It searches titles, people, genres, series, quotes, notes, tags and dialogue. A decade (“1990s”) or a date (“2026-07-14”) finds what you saved then. Open a result to share or edit it, or select several to tag or edit together.',
  'tour.step.search.name': 'Instant search',
  'tour.step.search.prose': 'Instant, {em1} search over everything you\'ve kept, with results grouped by what matched. From the Library or Catalogue it searches that side only.',
  'tour.step.search.title': 'Find any line again',
  'tour.step.share.blurb': 'share sheet (WhatsApp/Markdown/image cards) + Obsidian-friendly export',
  'tour.step.share.em1.label': 'image card',
  'tour.step.share.more': 'Share as Markdown, WhatsApp, plain text or Reddit, or as an image made on your device with a live preview. Export one work, a filtered set or the whole library as Markdown that imports back cleanly.',
  'tour.step.share.name': 'Share & export',
  'tour.step.share.prose': 'Any quote shares in one tap — as text, or as an {em1} drawn in your own skin.',
  'tour.step.share.title': 'Share a line, export the lot',
  'tour.step.staging.blurb': 'an import lands here first and is approved out of it',
  'tour.step.staging.em1.label': 'approve',
  'tour.step.staging.more': 'Fix a whole batch at once — which book, a speaker\'s name, a colour — then approve what you want and drop the rest. Nothing here is in your library yet.',
  'tour.step.staging.name': 'Imports waiting',
  'tour.step.staging.prose': 'Imports wait here until you {em1} them, so a bad import never reaches your library.',
  'tour.step.staging.title': 'Nothing lands unseen',
  'tour.step.stats.blurb': 'capture calendar, memory health, and author/actor/director/tag breakdowns',
  'tour.step.stats.more': 'Everything here opens something: a calendar dot shows that day\'s additions in Search, and any book, person or tag opens the same way.',
  'tour.step.stats.name': 'Stats',
  'tour.step.stats.prose': 'A calendar of what you\'ve saved, how well you remember it, and the people and tags you return to most.',
  'tour.step.stats.title': 'Your library in numbers',
  'tour.step.tags.blurb': 'cross-cutting tags with styles; pin your own PNG/SVG stickers to quotes',
  'tour.step.tags.em1.label': 'Stickers',
  'tour.step.tags.more': 'A tag can look like a sticker, banner, flyout, tape or reel, in any colour; renaming it updates every quote. Stickers are PNG or SVG files you upload; the quote\'s text flows around them, and you can drag them anywhere on the card.',
  'tour.step.tags.name': 'Tags & stickers',
  'tour.step.tags.prose': 'Tags work across books and films, each with its own look. {em1} are your own images, pinned to a quote like a seal.',
  'tour.step.tags.title': 'Tags & stickers',
  'tour.step.welcome.more': 'Next moves on, “skip tour” ends it, and “finish later” saves your place. The examples are built in, so none of your files are needed. The “?” in the top bar explains every control on the current screen and can replay the tour there.',
  'tour.step.welcome.prose': 'Tippani keeps the lines worth keeping — book highlights and film dialogue — with covers, tags, instant search and a daily memory quiz. This tour shows every feature.',
  'tour.step.welcome.title': 'Welcome to tippani',
